   "head_commit": {
    "id": "b12c9c6b829f9cf80a9ad6cf2d0c55f3530cd0d7",
    "message": "chore(reorg): plan R09 and R10 successor pair\n\nPlan the final two waves of the reorganization completion phase as one\nsuccessor pair against exact C0006 code fda296b20, mirroring the C0005 epoch\nthat planned the R04/R08 pair.\n\nB0011/R09 covers the 72 NumStability.Algorithms.TestMatrices.Higham28* owners\n(570 declarations, 41 destinations) in claude-lane. B0012/R10 covers the last\n18 NumStability.Algorithms.RandNLA* owners (225 declarations, 17 destinations);\nthe immutable scope freeze assigns those to codex-lane, so B0012 records that\nlane and claude-local operates it under a reviewed temporary authorization.\nCompleting the pair empties the unclassified ratchet.\n\nFrozen baseline projections P0011/P0012 and active common-base shared-file\nrequests R0012/R0013 accompany them. The 23- and 7-path requests intersect on\nexactly five integrator-owned files and are reconciled by the reviewed 25-path\ncommon-base union. The selection review records zero peer overlap across all\neight enforced dimensions.\n\nTwo contract amendments are included and separately reviewed:\n\n- destination_prefixes now admits exact rules, each required to name a path\n  absent at the branch base_sha. Prefix-only destinations could not express a\n  wave that adds a new canonical leaf beside already-complete siblings, since\n  claiming the directory collided with scope rows owned by no branch. An exact\n  rule authorizes one new file and nothing else, which is strictly narrower\n  than any prefix; all four overlap checks still apply, and prefix-only\n  records validate unchanged.\n\n- codex-lane may carry the reviewed B0012-scoped operator pair at C0006, using\n  the mechanism the contract already provides at C0003. The grant is\n  conditional on reviews/R10-operator-authorization.md being present with its\n  exact pinned bytes, and the decision is a pure function covered positively\n  and adversarially by the self-test.\n\nAll four reviewed planning documents are hash-pinned in both the branch\nrefresh evidence and C0006_REVIEW_FACTS, so neither rationale can drift from\nthe allowance it justifies.\n\nNeither wave is activated, no worker ref or worktree exists, and\nimplementation remains prohibited until this planned control passes Lean CI\nand a later activation control is green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
